---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<Prose title="Privacy Notice" description="How Wensum Black collects, uses and protects personal data under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018." h1="Privacy notice" eyebrow="Legal" updated="29 October 2026">
  <p>{site.legalName} ("we") is the controller of the personal data described here. Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or write to us at {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality} {site.address.postcode}.</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Booking details:</strong> your name, email, phone, pickup and destination, date, time, passenger count and any notes you give us.</li>
    <li><strong>Journey records:</strong> times, route and proof of delivery for courier jobs.</li>
    <li><strong>Website analytics:</strong> only if you accept analytics cookies. This is pseudonymous usage data collected by Google Analytics 4.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Why, and on what lawful basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To quote for and carry out your booking. Lawful basis: contract (Article 6(1)(b)).</li>
    <li>To keep the records that private hire licensing and tax law require. Lawful basis: legal obligation (Article 6(1)(c)).</li>
    <li>To understand how the site is used. Lawful basis: consent (Article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw consent at any time through Cookie settings in the footer.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share data with the driver assigned to your job, our email provider and our hosting provider (Vercel Inc.). If you consent to analytics, we also share it with Google Ireland Ltd. We never sell personal data or use it for advertising.</p>
  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>Some providers process data in the United States under the UK Extension to the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, or under standard contractual clauses.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep booking and journey records for six years for accounting purposes. We delete quote requests that do not become bookings after 12 months.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to access, correct, erase, restrict or object to the use of your data, and to data portability. Email us to use any of these rights. If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>
</Prose>
